winemac: one Metal shader cache folder per program, set before the first Metal device.

Metal keeps its shader cache (compiled MSL libraries and GPU pipeline binaries) in one folder per process identity,
here the loader's, shared by every program this engine runs, and MTLSetShaderCachePath takes another folder only
before the first Metal device exists; the Mac driver creates devices for the displays (cocoa_display.m) long before a
renderer loads, so a renderer cannot move it. The driver now sets highball/<program>/com.apple.metal under the
user's cache folder in macdrv_init, before the Cocoa side starts, the program being the Windows executable's name
(ntdll sets it with setprogname), as DXMT does per game on the Intel engines. One game's pipelines then survive the
others', and a second start compiles nothing Metal already compiled: in Microsoft Flight Simulator 2024 the second
boot's MTLCompilerService stayed at 0% where the first had it at 100 to 380% for the whole shader preparation.
HB_METAL_SHADER_CACHE names another folder (a relative one goes under the user's cache folder), 0 keeps Metal's
default. Measured on the M4 on 2026-10-15 (private/notes/msfs-2024-arm64-boot-2026-10-15.md).

